  "title": "Moysiacum",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 25 G1 Moysiacum",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/villa"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas seems to make a tentative association between the placename and the remains of <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../52087519\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">a possible Gallo-Roman villa</a> over which was built the later <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../552768118\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Church of Saint Martin at Moissac</a>, but the basis for this association is not clear.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A place mentioned in passing in the Vita of Saint Desiderius. Modern scholars have identified it with modern Moissac in southern France where there are significant Merovingian and later medieval remains, some of which overlie structures of late Roman date.",
  "reprPoint": [
    1.084339,
    44.103562
  ],
  "placeTypes": [
    "villa"
  ],
